  "passage": "Ken found a shortcut to school through a small alley. It looked faster on the map, so he tried it.\nAt first, it saved time. But after a week, road work began in the alley. He had to walk around machines, mud, and parked scooters. Sometimes he arrived later than before.\nHis sister laughed and called it \"the long shortcut.\"\nKen went back to his old route. It was not the shortest on the map, but it was clear, safe, and easy to walk.\nHe learned that faster is not always better. A good route is not only about distance. It is also about what happens along the way.",
